@host = http://localhost:5227

# =============================================================================
# GET /api/lenses
#
# No parameters, no body, always returns 200.
# Returns the lenses from calibration.json, each with its id, name and three
# weights. Its purpose: the client learns which lens ids are valid before it
# POSTs. The id is what gets stored and sent; the name is only ever displayed.
# =============================================================================

### The lenses the onboarding screen offers (Story 2.2)
GET {{host}}/api/lenses
Accept: application/json

### A route that does not exist — must return 404
GET {{host}}/api/lens
Accept: application/json

### The OpenAPI description of the API (Development only)
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

# =============================================================================
# POST /api/grades
#
# Send a food's nutrients per 100 g plus a lens name, get back the letter.
# No database, no auth: every request recomputes everything.
#
# The request passes four filters, in order. The first one that fails stops
# everything and returns 400:
#
#   1. The annotations on GradeRequestDto, run by [ApiController] BEFORE the
#      action. A missing required field or a negative value means the action
#      never runs. The nutrients are double? precisely so that an absent field
#      does not silently become 0.
#   2. The lens id, matched case-insensitively. Not found → 400 through
#      ValidationProblem, so it has exactly the same shape as the automatic
#      errors. lensId is the stable slug ("weight-loss"), never the display
#      name: renaming or translating a lens must not break saved references.
#   3. NutrientPlausibility.Check — energy against the macronutrients. Two ways
#      to fail: energy too high for any food (kilojoules sent as kilocalories),
#      or energy that does not follow from the protein, fat and carbohydrate.
#      This is why carbohydrate is required even though the engine never
#      scores it.
#   4. The engine: ScoreCombiner.Combine produces the score,
#      Calibration.GradeFor turns it into the letter.
#
# In the response:
#   grade: null       — a nutritionally empty food (water). NOT a bad grade;
#                       the product shows no letter at all.
#   isPartial /       — the engine worked with incomplete data: the component
#   isEstimated         was estimated, not measured.
#   the hidden rule   — a MEASURED density below the floor, on a food whose
#                       category has no rule → E, whatever the score is.
# =============================================================================

### Chicken breast under Weight Loss — 200, grade A
POST {{host}}/api/grades
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lensId": "weight-loss",
  "calories": 165, "protein": 31, "fat": 3.6, "fiber": 0,
  "saturatedFat": 1.0, "sodium": 74, "carbohydrate": 0,
  "potassium": 256, "magnesium": 29, "iron": 0.7, "calcium": 15, "vitaminC": 0
}

### The same food, a different lens — a different letter
POST {{host}}/api/grades
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lensId": "fitness",
  "calories": 165, "protein": 31, "fat": 3.6, "fiber": 0,
  "saturatedFat": 1.0, "sodium": 74, "carbohydrate": 0
}

### Filter 2 — a lens id that does not exist — 400, pointing at GET /api/lenses
POST {{host}}/api/grades
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lensId": "keto",
  "calories": 165, "protein": 31, "fat": 3.6, "fiber": 0,
  "saturatedFat": 1, "sodium": 74, "carbohydrate": 0
}

### Filter 1 — missing fields and a negative value — 400 with every error at once
POST {{host}}/api/grades
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lensId": "fitness", "calories": 165, "protein": -5 }

### Filter 3 — kilojoules sent as if they were kilocalories — 400
POST {{host}}/api/grades
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lensId": "fitness",
  "calories": 690, "protein": 31, "fat": 3.6, "fiber": 0,
  "saturatedFat": 1, "sodium": 74, "carbohydrate": 0
}

### Water — 200, but grade: null. No letter, not a bad letter.
POST {{host}}/api/grades
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lensId": "weight-loss",
  "calories": 0, "protein": 0, "fat": 0, "fiber": 0,
  "saturatedFat": 0, "sodium": 4, "carbohydrate": 0
}
